      "id": 1,
      "text": "Princeton was named for General Hugh Mercer, mortally wounded at the Battle of Princeton in 1777, and the town was settled in 1826.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Princeton-West-Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town became a key railroad hub on the Virginian Railway, carrying coal and goods through the Appalachian mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
